    "durationMs": 255555,
    "finalText": "The URL shortener is complete and fully tested. Here's what I built:\n\n**Stack**: axum 0.8.4 + sqlx (PostgreSQL) + tokio, with the `links` table (`id BIGSERIAL`, unique `code`, `url`, `clicks`, `created_at`) created by an embedded migration (`migrations/0001_create_links.sql`) that `sqlx::migrate!` applies at startup — so `sh start.sh` applies pending migrations then serves in the foreground on `0.0.0.0:8000` (it uses the prebuilt release binary, rebuilding only if missing).\n\n**Behavior verified end-to-end with live HTTP tests:**\n- `POST /links` → 201 `{\"code\",\"url\",\"clicks\":0}`, URL returned/stored unchanged; auto-generated 8-char codes (regenerated on the astronomically-unlikely collision); custom codes validated against 4–20 ASCII `[A-Za-z0-9_-]`\n- Duplicate custom code → 409, unknown codes on `GET /links/{code}` and `GET /r/{code}` → 404 JSON\n- `GET /r/{code}` → 302 with exact `Location` header, clicks incremented atomically via `UPDATE ... clicks = clicks + 1 RETURNING url` (exactly once per request — confirmed 3 hits → 3 clicks)\n- `GET /links` → `{\"items\": [...], \"total\": n}` in ascending creation order\n- All failure modes → 422 JSON `{\"error\": ...}`: malformed JSON, missing/null/non-string url, relative URLs, non-http(s) schemes, empty host, and invalid codes (too short/long, bad chars) — handled by a custom JSON extractor that maps every body problem to 422\n- Restart persistence: killed the server, restarted via `sh start.sh` — all links and click counts survived and kept incrementing\n\nI also truncated the `links` table afterward, so the database is empty and clean for the automated test suite. README includes the startup instructions (`DATABASE_URL` from the environment, `sh start.sh`)."
